#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/ml/foundations/hello-blazeface.rst:2
msgid "Hello BlazeFace"
msgstr "Hello BlazeFace"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/ml/foundations/hello-blazeface.rst:4
msgid ""
"*BlazeFace* is a face-detection neural network from Google's MediaPipe "
"collection. A single inference call returns a bounding rectangle around each"
" detected face along with six facial landmarks -- right eye, left eye, nose,"
" mouth, right ear, left ear. Every OpenMV Cam that ships with neural-network"
" support carries the :data:`blazeface_front_128.tflite` model on flash, so "
"running an end-to-end face detector takes a few lines of Python."
msgstr ""
"*BlazeFace* je neuronska mreža za detekciju lica iz Googleove zbirke "
"MediaPipe. Jedan poziv zaključivanja vraća granični pravokutnik oko svakog "
"detektiranog lica zajedno sa šest orijentira lica -- desno oko, lijevo oko, "
"nos, usta, desno uho, lijevo uho. Svaki OpenMV Cam koji se isporučuje s "
"podrškom za neuronske mreže nosi model :data:`blazeface_front_128.tflite` na"
" flash memoriji, pa pokretanje cjelovitog detektora lica zahtijeva svega "
"nekoliko redaka Pythona."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/ml/foundations/hello-blazeface.rst:13
msgid "The full script"
msgstr "Cijela skripta"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/ml/foundations/hello-blazeface.rst:36
msgid ""
"That is the entire face detector. There is nothing else to it; the script "
"captures a frame, hands it to the model, walks the returned list of "
"detections, and draws each face's bounding rectangle plus its six landmarks "
"back into the frame. The IDE preview shows the boxes and landmarks in real "
"time."
msgstr ""
"To je cijeli detektor lica. Nema ničeg drugog u njemu; skripta hvata "
"sličicu, predaje je modelu, prolazi vraćeni popis detekcija i crta granični "
"pravokutnik svakog lica te njegovih šest orijentira natrag u sličicu. "
"Pretpregled u IDE-u u stvarnom vremenu prikazuje okvire i orijentire."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/ml/foundations/hello-blazeface.rst:43
msgid "What each line does"
msgstr "Što svaki redak radi"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/ml/foundations/hello-blazeface.rst:45
msgid ""
"The first three lines import the modules the script needs. :mod:`csi` is the"
" camera-sensor interface; :mod:`ml` is the machine-learning module the rest "
"of this chapter is about; :class:`~ml.postprocessing.mediapipe.BlazeFace` is"
" the post-processor that turns BlazeFace's raw output tensors into the "
"bounding-box and landmark list the script iterates over."
msgstr ""
"Prva tri retka uvoze module koje skripta treba. :mod:`csi` je sučelje "
"senzora kamere; :mod:`ml` je modul za strojno učenje o kojem govori ostatak "
"ovog poglavlja; :class:`~ml.postprocessing.mediapipe.BlazeFace` je naknadni "
"obrađivač koji BlazeFaceove sirove izlazne tenzore pretvara u popis "
"graničnih okvira i orijentira kroz koji skripta iterira."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/ml/foundations/hello-blazeface.rst:52
msgid ""
"The next five lines configure the sensor. The camera is reset to a known "
"state, set to RGB565 colour, set to VGA resolution, and then *windowed* to a"
" 400-by-400 square. The window matters: BlazeFace was trained on square "
"crops, and giving it a square input lines up the network's expected aspect "
"ratio with what it sees in the captured frame."
msgstr ""
"Sljedećih pet redaka konfigurira senzor. Kamera se resetira u poznato "
"stanje, postavlja na RGB565 boju, postavlja na VGA razlučivost i zatim "
"*prozoruje* na kvadrat 400 puta 400. Prozor je važan: BlazeFace je treniran "
"na kvadratnim izrezima, a davanje kvadratnog ulaza poravnava mrežin "
"očekivani omjer širine i visine s onim što vidi u uhvaćenoj sličici."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/ml/foundations/hello-blazeface.rst:59
msgid "The model-loading line opens the model file:"
msgstr "Redak za učitavanje modela otvara datoteku modela:"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/ml/foundations/hello-blazeface.rst:66
msgid ""
":class:`ml.Model` reads the file at the given path -- ``/rom/`` is a flash-"
"resident filesystem covered later -- and returns a model object the script "
"will run inferences against. The ``postprocess=`` keyword registers the "
"BlazeFace post-processor; without it, ``predict`` would return the network's"
" raw output tensors and the application would have to decode them by hand. "
"With it, ``predict`` returns the decoded result directly. The "
"``threshold=0.4`` argument on the post-processor sets the minimum confidence"
" the network must report before a detection is kept; lower values catch "
"fainter faces at the cost of more false positives."
msgstr ""
":class:`ml.Model` čita datoteku na danoj putanji -- ``/rom/`` je datotečni "
"sustav smješten u flashu, obrađen kasnije -- i vraća objekt modela nad kojim"
" će skripta pokretati zaključivanja. Ključna riječ ``postprocess=`` "
"registrira BlazeFace naknadni obrađivač; bez nje, ``predict`` bi vratio "
"mrežine sirove izlazne tenzore i aplikacija bi ih morala ručno dekodirati. S"
" njom, ``predict`` izravno vraća dekodirani rezultat. Argument "
"``threshold=0.4`` na naknadnom obrađivaču postavlja minimalnu pouzdanost "
"koju mreža mora prijaviti prije nego se detekcija zadrži; niže vrijednosti "
"hvataju slabija lica po cijenu više lažno pozitivnih."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/ml/foundations/hello-blazeface.rst:77
msgid ""
"The remaining four lines are the main loop. Each pass through it captures "
"one frame and asks the model what it sees:"
msgstr ""
"Preostala četiri retka su glavna petlja. Svaki prolaz kroz nju hvata jednu "
"sličicu i pita model što vidi:"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/ml/foundations/hello-blazeface.rst:87
msgid ""
":meth:`~ml.Model.predict` takes a list of inputs (here, one captured image) "
"and returns a list of detection tuples. Each tuple holds the bounding "
"rectangle ``(x, y, w, h)``, a confidence ``score`` between zero and one, and"
" a ``(6, 2)`` :class:`~ulab.numpy.ndarray` of landmark coordinates -- the "
"right eye, left eye, nose, mouth, right ear, and left ear in that order. The"
" drawing call uses :meth:`~image.Image.draw_rectangle` -- the same primitive"
" every classical detector in the image chapter ended with -- to outline the "
"face. :func:`ml.utils.draw_keypoints` is a small helper from the ml "
"utilities that marks each keypoint with a cross at its ``(x, y)`` position."
msgstr ""
":meth:`~ml.Model.predict` uzima popis ulaza (ovdje, jednu uhvaćenu sliku) i "
"vraća popis n-torki detekcija. Svaka n-torka drži granični pravokutnik ``(x,"
" y, w, h)``\\ , pouzdanost ``score`` između nule i jedan, te ``(6, 2)`` "
":class:`~ulab.numpy.ndarray` koordinata orijentira -- desno oko, lijevo oko,"
" nos, usta, desno uho i lijevo uho tim redoslijedom. Poziv za crtanje "
"koristi :meth:`~image.Image.draw_rectangle` -- isti primitiv kojim je "
"završavao svaki klasični detektor u poglavlju o slici -- za ocrtavanje lica."
" :func:`ml.utils.draw_keypoints` je mali pomoćnik iz ml uslužnih alata koji "
"svaku ključnu točku označava križićem na njezinoj ``(x, y)`` poziciji."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/ml/foundations/hello-blazeface.rst:100
msgid "What the script does not say"
msgstr "Što skripta ne kaže"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/ml/foundations/hello-blazeface.rst:102
msgid ""
"The script is seven runnable lines of inference work past the imports and "
"the sensor setup, but a great deal of arithmetic happens inside those seven "
"lines. The captured 400-by-400 RGB565 frame becomes a 128-by-128 quantized "
"8-bit tensor before reaching the network; the network runs hundreds of "
"operations against tens of thousands of weights; the resulting tensors of "
"confidence scores and box offsets become a ranked list of non-overlapping "
"bounding boxes with attached landmarks before ``predict`` returns. Every one"
" of those transformations is something the application *can* control if it "
"needs to, and several of them have to be tuned for any non-default model."
msgstr ""
"Skripta je sedam izvedivih redaka zaključivanja nakon uvoza i postavljanja "
"senzora, no unutar tih sedam redaka odvija se velika količina aritmetike. "
"Uhvaćena RGB565 sličica 400 puta 400 postaje kvantizirani 8-bitni tenzor 128"
" puta 128 prije nego dođe do mreže; mreža izvodi stotine operacija nad "
"desecima tisuća težina; nastali tenzori pouzdanosti i pomaka okvira postaju "
"rangirani popis nepreklapajućih graničnih okvira s pridruženim orijentirima "
"prije nego ``predict`` vrati. Svaka od tih transformacija nešto je što "
"aplikacija *može* kontrolirati ako treba, a nekoliko ih se mora ugoditi za "
"bilo koji nezadani model."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/ml/foundations/hello-blazeface.rst:114
msgid "The next four subsections walk those transformations open. In order:"
msgstr "Sljedeća četiri pododjeljka razlažu te transformacije. Redom:"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/ml/foundations/hello-blazeface.rst:116
msgid ""
"*The ml module* -- what :class:`ml.Model` exposes once a model is loaded, "
"and where the model file actually lives on the cam."
msgstr ""
"*The ml module* -- što :class:`ml.Model` izlaže kada se model učita, i gdje "
"datoteka modela zapravo živi na kameri."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/ml/foundations/hello-blazeface.rst:118
msgid ""
"*The inference pipeline* -- the four stages of every "
":meth:`~ml.Model.predict` call."
msgstr ""
"*The inference pipeline* -- četiri stadija svakog :meth:`~ml.Model.predict` "
"poziva."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/ml/foundations/hello-blazeface.rst:120
msgid ""
"*Inference engines* -- the CPU and NPU paths that run the network's "
"arithmetic."
msgstr ""
"*Inference engines* -- CPU i NPU putovi koji izvode mrežinu aritmetiku."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/ml/foundations/hello-blazeface.rst:122
msgid ""
"*Decoding the output* -- the post-processors that convert raw output tensors"
" into the detections this script iterated over."
msgstr ""
"*Decoding the output* -- naknadni obrađivači koji sirove izlazne tenzore "
"pretvaraju u detekcije kroz koje je ova skripta iterirala."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/ml/foundations/hello-blazeface.rst:125
msgid ""
"By the end of the chapter the reader can write the equivalent script for a "
"model that did not ship with the cam, decode a tensor whose post-processor "
"does not exist yet, and reason about why a particular model runs at 30 FPS "
"on one cam and 3 FPS on another."
msgstr ""
"Do kraja poglavlja čitatelj može napisati ekvivalentnu skriptu za model koji"
" nije isporučen s kamerom, dekodirati tenzor čiji naknadni obrađivač još ne "
"postoji, i razumjeti zašto određeni model radi pri 30 FPS na jednoj kameri, "
"a 3 FPS na drugoj."
